  "id": "interrogative-suggestibility",
  "term": "interrogative suggestibility",
  "definition": "Interrogative suggestibility is the degree to which a person’s responses are influenced by messages conveyed during formal questioning in a closed social interaction. In psychology, it refers to how questioning can shape or alter an individual’s answers.",
